# Log-triage — parallel Go goroutine dump
#
# Exercises the parallel Errors[] slice in the schema: multiple
# goroutines at time of crash map to peer entries in Errors[], not
# to Cause chains. The LLM should emit 3 errors (one per goroutine).
ID="logtri_goroutine_dump"
NAME="log-triage Go concurrent map writes — parallel goroutines"
QUESTION="哪些 goroutine 同时出错？它们的共同问题是什么？"
LOG='fatal error: concurrent map writes

goroutine 15 [running]:
runtime.throw({0x123, 0x5})
	/usr/local/go/src/runtime/panic.go:1047 +0x5d
runtime.mapassign_faststr(0x0, 0x0, {0x0, 0x0})
	/usr/local/go/src/runtime/map_faststr.go:212 +0x37e
main.writeSession(0x0, {0x140000a2080, 0x8})
	internal/agent/analyzer.go:100 +0x1e

goroutine 87 [running]:
main.writeSession(0x0, {0x140000a2088, 0x8})
	internal/agent/analyzer.go:100 +0x1e

goroutine 120 [running]:
main.writeSession(0x0, {0x140000a2090, 0x8})
	internal/agent/analyzer.go:100 +0x1e
'
# 2026-05-08: drop EXPECT_CONTAINS="concurrent" (English-only literal
# substring) — model answered correctly in Chinese ("并发写入 map")
# but the literal-match flagged FAIL. Move "concurrent" into the
# regex channel alongside its Chinese equivalents so the case
# accepts either language. "map" stays as a literal anchor (the
# data-structure name is universal). "race" stays as the broad
# vocabulary alternation (race / race condition / data race /
# 竞态 / 数据竞争 / 竞争).
EXPECT_SECTIONS="map"
# 2026-05-09 third-pass broaden: model said "BugClassRace" (CamelCase
# typed enum value) + "并发 map 写操作" — semantically correct race-
# condition identification but neither matched lowercase "race" alt
# nor Chinese 竞争 alt. Add: [Rr]ace alternative (catches Go enum
# names like BugClassRace), 并发.*写 (semantic "concurrent write"
# pattern that maps to race).
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="concurrent|并发
race|race condition|data race|竞态|数据竞争|竞争|[Rr]ace|并发.*写"
